/-
**Test only** (the NON-VACUITY rule; kitgen's `NonVacuityLinked.lean`): the one hypothesis-class
premise of rabia's statement (`Dsverify/Spec/rabia/examples/rabianet/TopLevelRobustness.lean`),
go-redis v8's `InitHyp` (its initializer kept a premise, dsv-fix3), has an instance, built as a
`theorem` (no `instance` of an `InitHyp` anywhere: etc/dsv/README.md): its initializer's walk
(`Dsverify/Proof/github_com/go_redis/redis/v8/InitInstancesLinked.lean`, generated by
`etc/dsv/tools/inithyp-instances.py`), over local axioms for its names-only initializers. (Until
dsv-fix4 also the classes `zerolog.Hyps`, gogo `proto.Hyps`, `math.rand.Hyps` and
`os.signal.NoSignals quietSigs`, from local axioms here: they are per-function trust-boundary axioms
now, and the proof discharges them.) No statement or proof imports this module: its local axioms are
in no trust base.
-/
module

public import Dsverify.Spec.rabia.examples.rabianet.TopLevelRobustness
public import Dsverify.Proof.github_com.go_redis.redis.v8.InitInstancesLinked

@[expose] public section

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

namespace Perennial
namespace rabia.examples.rabianet.instances

open Iris Iris.BI Iris.ProgramLogic Iris.Std Iris.ProofMode

section statement
open github_com.mit_pdos.etcd_grove.examples.lib.remote.counter (remoteGF)
attribute [local instance] Net.netExts Net.netExtsSemantics Net.netExtsInterp Net.netExts_hasNet
variable [GoGlobalContext] [lctx : GoLocalContext] [go.Semantics]
variable [github_com.go_redis.redis.v8.Assumptions]

/-- **The non-vacuity instance** (the NON-VACUITY rule): rabia's hypothesis-class premise, in the
statement's own form (`rabia_remote_robust.spec`: at `remoteGF` and every machine's heap). -/
theorem nonvacuous_premises : ∀ G L, letI := heapAt G L;
    github_com.go_redis.redis.v8.InitHyp remoteGF := by
  intro G L
  exact github_com.go_redis.redis.v8.initHyp_holds (GF := remoteGF) (hG := heapAt G L)

end statement

end rabia.examples.rabianet.instances
end Perennial
